Hi all

I just got to wondering what is the deciding factor for splitting words into
syllables?  On page 22 of *.i la lojban. mo*, about halfway through the
section on brivla, is an explanation that reads:

The consonant cluster rule has the qualification that the letter y is
> totally ignored, even if it splits a consonant cluster. Thus lobypei/LOBE,uh,pay/ is a
> *brivla* even though the y separates the bp cluster.


 Yet there is also a rule that claims brivla are penultemately stressed.
Surely then, it should be */lobe,UH,pay/*, not */LOBE,uh,pay/*?

Cheers!
Johan

